/target
# PGO build artifacts (scripts/pgo_build.sh + scripts/pgo_wheel.sh):
# per-phase target dirs, raw profiles, merged profdata, identity traces.
/target-pgo*
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# cargo-mutants default output dir (transient mutation-testing artifacts;
# real runs write under /tmp via --output). See .cargo/mutants.toml.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# maturin / Python build artifacts
*.so
*.pyd
*.dylib
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
dist/
wheels/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# bv (beads viewer) local config and caches
.bv/

# Claude Code: track shared project config under .claude (skills, commands,
# settings.json, settings.local.json). Ignore runtime worktrees + backups.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/commands/**
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/hooks/**
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/**/*.bak

# Agent-flywheel local state (per-machine)
.pi-flywheel/
.ntm/human_inbox/
.ntm/logs/*--inflight-resume.log
.ntm/logs/*--inflight.log
.ntm/summaries/*.json
.ntm/rate_limits.json

# Local agent/IDE MCP bridge configs (may contain local bearer tokens)
.antigravitycli/
cline.mcp.json
cursor.mcp.json
gemini.mcp.json
opencode.json
windsurf.mcp.json

# br recovery WAL artifacts (transient — regenerated by br on restart)
.beads/.br_recovery/

# Local CLI capture logs (regenerate via ./target/debug/sts2-cli > log.txt)
example_cli_log.txt
*_cli_log.txt

# Bead sts2-rs-yuyc: MCTS A/B + oracle data artifacts (generated;
# regenerate via `cargo run --release --example mcts_corpus` etc.).
# `.gitkeep` + README inside `data/` are tracked.
/crates/sts2-bench/data/*.json
.env

# skill-creator eval scratch (throwaway)
.claude/skills/*-workspace/

# Parity-sweep manifests: machine-generated per-run snapshots
# (regenerable; comparator reads them from the local filesystem, not git).
docs/audits/sweeps/*-manifest.json

# Unpacked .run corpus (regenerated from the committed git-lfs bundle
# data/run-corpus/files.tar.zst via data/run-corpus/unpack.sh).
data/run-corpus/files/

# Phase 2 expert-iteration round artifacts (large NPZ corpora + net JSONs)
expi/

# Combat surrogate prototype data + model artifacts (generated;
# regenerate via combat_surrogate_data + train_combat_surrogate.py).
data/runai/surrogate/

# Potion-weight A/B run reports + logs (issue #253; regenerate via
# scripts/potion_weight_ab.sh). Scripts + the release-300 panel are tracked.
experiments/potion-weight-ab/

# Legacy guard: run_arena's --out default used to be a bare "report.jsonl", so
# any sweep run from this directory dropped scratch right here. One such file
# was committed by accident in 303b73508 and nothing ever read it, so every
# later sweep surfaced as spurious dirt in `git status`. The default now writes
# under target/ (already ignored), but keep this so an older binary — or the
# file already sitting in working copies — stays out of the index.
/report.jsonl

# Harvested combat-fixture pool (logs/2026-08-12-fixture-pool/harvest.sh).
# ~4000 generated scenario TOMLs; regenerable in ~10 min per character. The
# derived position book is the committed artifact, not the raw pool. Lives
# under the repo rather than /tmp because the /tmp copy has been wiped twice,
# blocking the 2026-05-20 GH #17 A/B and forcing synthetic decks elsewhere.
data/run-fixtures/
# Disjoint-seed twin of the pool above, harvested so a policy prior can be
# trained without seeing the positions the book scores it on. Same rationale:
# regenerable, large, never reviewed.
data/run-fixtures-train/
# Belt-carrying twin (`EXPORT_POTIONS=1 harvest.sh`, GH #446): the frozen v1/v2
# books and the dominance suite pin the state_hash of the belt-LESS pool above,
# so the potion pool is a separate directory the v3 book is built from.
data/run-fixtures-potions/
# Hard pool (`just harvest-fixtures-hard`, GH #446): three sub-pools
# (ascension 10 / 40-HP snapshot) the playout-selected book is built from.
data/run-fixtures-hard/
# Disjoint-seed pool the fitted rollout priority table trains on
# (`just harvest-fixtures-rollout`, GH #805).
data/run-fixtures-rollout/

# MCTS high-ascension (A8-A10) campaign. The loose files stay out of git; the
# whole campaign — fixture pool AND raw result rows — is committed instead as
# the single LFS bundle logs/2026-08-15-highasc-pool/campaign-artifacts.tar.zst
# (828K packed, ~28M unpacked). Restore it with that directory's unpack.sh,
# repack with pack.sh. NOT regenerable in practice: the pool needed a god-mode
# generator path that hangs reproducibly (bead sts2-rs-19oq0), and the result
# rows are the evidence behind the PR #467 win-rate claims.
data/asc-fixture-pool/
logs/2026-08-15-highasc-pool/*
!logs/2026-08-15-highasc-pool/campaign-artifacts.tar.zst
!logs/2026-08-15-highasc-pool/pack.sh
!logs/2026-08-15-highasc-pool/unpack.sh
!logs/2026-08-15-highasc-pool/README.md
!logs/2026-08-15-highasc-pool/depth-ladder.md
!logs/2026-08-15-highasc-pool/endturn-widening-findings.md
